From: Zachary Vorhies <zachvorhies@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:46:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(watcher): notify main thread once per interrupt (#1616)

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/zackees/zccache/commit/64b7e7c88eb52d09abbea410071a8a8fd2f0acf9]

Let the dispatch loop own worker KeyboardInterrupt notification so
predicate failures cannot leak a second interrupt into pytest.

FileWatcher._predicate_allows() called handle_keyboard_interrupt() (a
real _thread.interrupt_main()) and then re-raised into _dispatch_loop(),
whose own except clause called it again, so one predicate interrupt
could reach the main thread twice. The tests also let the real
interrupt_main() fire and expected to catch it in an assertRaises block
entered only after file_path.write_text("b\n"); NativeWatcher.poll_batch
blocks while holding the GIL, so the main thread could still be inside
write_text when the interrupt arrived, and the KeyboardInterrupt aborted
the whole pytest session (exit code 2, "!!! KeyboardInterrupt !!!" after
every reported test passed). The tests now keep interrupt_main mocked
until the watcher has stopped and assert it was called exactly once.

Fixes https://github.com/zackees/zccache/issues/1615
